    "updated_at": "2017-09-11T14:55:34Z",
    "body": "OK, changed to:\r\n\r\n> <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-content-nothing\" id=\"the-template-element:concept-content-nothing\">Nothing</a> (see prose).\r\n\r\nBut I think it could also be reasonable to change it to:\r\n\r\n> <a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-content-nothing\" id=\"the-template-element:concept-content-nothing\">Nothing</a> (<a href=\"https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#no-browsing-context\">no conformance requirements</a>).\r\n\r\nThat is, just hoist up the sentence *The template contents have no \\_conformance requirements\\_.*  from the prose below that we’re otherwise, with the *“(see prose)“* text, directing readers to see.\r\n\r\nIf we were to hoist it up there that way, we should then just drop that sentence from the prose below (because it would then simply be redundant).\r\n\r\nAnd for the record here to be clear: The \\_conformance requirements\\_ link text goes to this language:\r\n\r\n> DOM nodes whose node document does not have a browsing context are exempt from all document conformance requirements other than the HTML syntax requirements and XML syntax requirements.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
