    "updated_at": "2017-09-12T09:52:33Z",
    "body": "> I have two problems with this PR:\r\n>\r\n> 2. I think this change ends up being confusing since the normative prose doesn't say anything about the content model. It's only the example that mentions it. So at best we could say something \"see example for clarification\".\r\n\r\nOK, in 2f2844a I’ve changed it to *\\_Nothing\\_ (for clarification, \\_see example\\_).*, where *\\_see example\\_* is a link to the example.\r\n\r\n> 1. It claims to fix an issue, but I don't think it fixes it since the issue is also about the \"Writing HTML\" section.\r\n\r\nI’ll make time to try to add something myself here for it to the \"Writing HTML\" section—unless @zcorpan has some time to do it",
